{
  "challenges": [
    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_pat_182",
      "name": "failure-report",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Build a failure report that points to the cause",
      "description": "After a bad deploy the CI summary listed 40 failures as `assert 500 == 201`, each with a different order id, nobody could find the matching server logs, and one report pasted a customer's refresh token into a Slack channel. The editor holds `tests/report.py` with its key blocks missing, each marked by a `# [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so the report keeps, for each failed test, the request, its path template, the status, the server's `X-Request-Id` and the error title; hides every credential in headers and bodies; groups failures by root cause (same endpoint template, status and error), biggest group first; and lists tests that passed on a rerun as flaky, not as failures. The docstring is the exact contract.",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "outcomes": [
        "reliable-suites"
      ],
      "points": 30,
      "hints": [
        "Read the report the way the on-call engineer would: which line tells them it is one bug and not forty, and which value lets them find the request in the server logs?",
        "Look at the path segments that differ between failures (numbers, UUIDs, the query string), at where a token can hide (headers, nested JSON keys, plain-text bodies), and at the outcome of each test's last attempt.",
        "Grouping log lines of a worker: `key = f\"{job_type} {queue_template} -> {exit_code}\"`, `groups.setdefault(key, []).append(line)`, then `sorted(groups.items(), key=lambda kv: (-len(kv[1]), kv[0]))`; a token in `{\"auth\": {\"token\": ...}}` is found by walking dicts and lists recursively."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "python",
        "filePath": "tests/report.py",
        "executionMode": "stdio",
        "timeLimitMs": 3000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
      "tests": [
        {
